/* Movie Night — dataset (v5). Each movie carries a 0-10 taste vector on ten axes:
   adrenaline, brainy, scary, funny, heartwarming, dark, romantic, epic, cozy, weird.
   Entries with tier "core" are hand-written. Entries with tier "catalog" were
   sourced from Wikipedia year/genre categories: director and runtime come from
   the film's infobox (runtime is null when unknown — never invented), the
   description is adapted from the film's Wikipedia lead (CC BY-SA), and the
   taste vector is an ESTIMATE derived from genre-baseline profiles.
   Catalog additions are Wikipedia-notable films: selection used article
   substance (length), a confirmed poster and a real lead extract as the
   notability proxy — there are no external ratings (e.g. Rotten Tomatoes)
   in this dataset. The v5 expansion pass prioritized American productions
   from 2000-2026 (origin = Wikipedia category evidence), capped other
   foreign productions at a small minority of additions, and applied the
   documented Indian-production exclusion to every addition. Genre tags
   in the refined taxonomy come from Wikipedia category evidence or the
   derived-label rules documented in the README.
   Poster URLs come from the Wikipedia API (existence confirmed via the
   API at build time); an empty poster means the UI draws an elegant
   generated cover instead. */
